{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206796-3e-dragonblooded-firearms-charms","id":1206796,"title":"3e Dragonblooded Firearms charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-13T23:01:32-07:00","id":1206796,"title":"3e Dragonblooded Firearms charms","content":"I need them for my own upcoming game in Modern, so I just converted them.<br /> <br /> This set follows the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/722019-guns-guns-guns-3e-firearms-homebrew\">homebrew guns</a> I made, meaning guns use the Archery ability and these charms just expand upon it into a little sub tree. It also uses the Strong/Special type opponent split done in my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1021837-3e-bestiary-guide-version-1-0\">Monster Guide</a>, but that can be ignored if you want.<br /> <br /> I also never made DB charms before so this'll be fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">ELEMENTAL DRAGON BULLET</span><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: 4m\u037e <b>Mins\u200b</b>: Archery 2 Essence 1\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords\u200b</b>: Dual<br /> <b>Duration\u200b</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite charm</b>s\u200b: Unobstructed Hunter\u2019s Aim<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded\u2019s anima leaps from her to her bullet as it flies towards its unfortunate foe, imbuing it with elemental power. This charm works the same as Elemental Bolt Attack minus the ability of using anima for a range increase (Dragonblooded page 218). Air Elemental Dragon Bullet and Death from Nowhere do not stack.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">ARC OF THE DRAGON</span><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: 2m\u037e <b>Mins\u200b</b>: Archery 4 Essence 2\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords\u200b</b>: Air, Uniform<br /> <b>Duration\u200b</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Elemental Dragon Bullet<br /> <br /> The lash of energy that arcs from the Scion\u2019s weapons quickly leaps towards another nearby opponent. This charm can supplement an attack with any energy-based weapon. If the attack successfully hits and damages the opponent then the attack arcs out towards another opponent nearby in close range. The attack roll is the same as the one that hit the initial target and the damage is the amount of 10s in the attack roll in unsoakable <b>withering </b>dice to a maximum of (Essence or Perception, lower) dice. The Dragonblooded does not gain initiative except that gained from initiative crash. Against Strong type opponents you may use the 10s across both the attack and damage rolls.<br /> <br /> If the Dragonblood has an Air aura active, he may take the 10s in his attack and damage roll any uses the higher of the two values.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">BLAZING BULLSEYE ATTACK</span><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: 3m 1WP\u037e <b>Mins\u200b</b>: Archery 3 Essence 2\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Simple<br /> <b>Keywords\u200b</b>: Air/Fire, Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration\u200b</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Elemental Dragon Bullet<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded\u2019s bullet engulfs the enemy in a spectral flame, which its cold touch foreshadows the pain that is about to come. This charm is a gambit in order to ignite the enemy that carries a difficulty of 3. If the gambit succeeds the opponent is engulfed in a ghostly blue flame which illuminates them as if they had a glowing anima banner and confers an amount of aiming dice equal to the Dragonblooded\u2019s (Essence/2, round up) to all allied attacks. These aim dice do not count as dice from charm, but are still subject to the 3 dice maximum from aiming and targets still need to aim normally when attacking from medium or longer (Although they gain the bonus dice from this charm if eligible). Lastly charms that work when aiming (Such as Death from Nowhere) still need an aim action to work.<br /> <br /> While in Air or Fire aura, the Dragon-blooded may instead make a normal decisive attack with this Charm. If this attack deals three or more levels of damage, the target is engulfed in ghostly flame as if the user had succeeded on the gambit.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">DRAWING THE DRAGON\u2019S FURY</span><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: +1a\u037e <b>Mins\u200b</b>: Archery 4 Essence 2\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords\u200b</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration\u200b</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Elemental Dragon Bullet<br /> <br /> The scion of the elements wrath becomes so potent that his shot becomes infused with the wrath of two dragons. By paying a surcharge of 1a to the cost of Elemental Dragon Bullet the Dragonblooded can infuse it with two elemental powers instead of one. The Dragonblooded must have access to such elements in order to use them (Meaning they must\u2019ve have been purchased).<br /> <br /> This charm can be used at Bonfire, but one of the elements chosen must be the Dragonblooded\u2019s native aspect.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">RED HOT DEMOLITION ROUND</span><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: 4m\u037e <b>Mins\u200b</b>: Archery 3 Essence 2\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: Fire<br /> <b>Duration\u200b</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Elemental Dragon Bullet<br /> <br /> The bullets of the children of Hesiesh sear the air and battlefield, a trail of devastation that makes clear who their target is. A Dragonblooded may use this charm in order to make a ranged Feat of Strength check in order to destroy any cover their opponents may be behind. The roll is the same as normal, but the effective strength of the Dragonblooded varies on the weapon held: Light and Medium firearms have an effective strength of 3, heavy firearms have a strength of 5, bows use whatever the user\u2019s natural strength is. Any charms Feat of Strength charm can validly boost this roll. Don\u2019t forget to add the tool bonus to the roll too!<br /> <br /> Unless a piece of cover is somehow moving, a Dragonblooded generally doesn\u2019t need a roll to hit the target, but if such a thing is needed then the difficulty is set based on the Storyteller. Lastly this charm is capable of blowing away pieces of cover. If you\u2019re having a Firefight in a bank and a shooter is around the corner you don\u2019t need to make a Feat of Strength to bring down the entire building, just enough to blow off a piece of the wall.<br /> <br /> At Essence 3+ this charm can be repurchased, for a surcharge of 1WP may activate this charm in which if the Dragonblooded successfully destroys a piece of cover then an area of close around the piece of cover immediately catches fire. This fire lasts for the rest of the scene and may spread if other flammable materials are nearby. In environments that are ill suited for open flames (Underwater, vacuum) the flames last a single turn before going out. The charm may also be fired at a target with no cover nearby in order to catch an area on fire.<br /> <br /> When the user has Fire Aura active and the shot is enough to destroy a piece of cover the cover then explodes, damaging everything in the area as if hit by a medium explosion. If the Dragonblooded has the repurchase then cover that is indestructible isn\u2019t destroyed but has the area around it immediately catch fire if the Feat of Strength roll would be enough to destroy the piece of cover if it were made of normal materials.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">MOLTEN DOORWAY BULLET</span><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: 5m\u037e <b>Mins\u200b</b>: Archery 5 Essence 3\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords\u200b</b>: Fire/Wood, Decisive-Only<br /> <b>Duration\u200b</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Red Hot Demolition Round x2<br /> <br /> A red ember sits in the barrel of the Exalt\u2019s gun, long instants before the hammer sparks the round on its explosive journey. When it does, that hungry fire persists, an orange streak sinking to the heart of an opponent in the Terrestrial\u2019s path. This charm enhances a <b>decisive </b>attack in which the red hot bullet becomes embedded within the opponent\u2019s flesh. This bullet has the statistics of (Essence/2, round up)i/turn (lethal in crash), -(ESS/2, round up) penalty, and lasts for (Perception or Essence, whichever is higher) turns. One needs to physically removed the bullet in order to rid oneself of a poison, in which a miscellaneous action to make a roll of DEXTERITY+MEDICINE with a difficulty of the Dragonblooded\u2019s (Essence) is needed to remove it safely. Despite using a poison statline this attack isn\u2019t a poison, but rather a physical thing.<br /> <br /> This bullet is particularly devastating to Wood elementals, gods, demons, or anything strongly related to wood (minus Wood aspects). The damage in such case the damage becomes aggravated immediately. If the Dragonblooded is within aura then 10s on the resistance roll are counted as a single success.<br /> <br /> This charm can be used with bows, in which case it gains the Wood keyword. In Vanilla games this charm is often called \u201cFangs of the Wood Dragon\u201d. It returns the anti-wood properties.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">PENETRATING SHELL PRECISION</span><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: 5m\u037e <b>Mins\u200b</b>: Archery 4 Essence 2\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Simple<br /> <b>Keywords\u200b</b>: Fire, Uniform<br /> <b>Duration\u200b</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Elemental Dragon Bullet<br /> <br /> A superheated round is combined with superhuman reflexes and uncanny timing, allowing the Dragonblooded to shoot through multiple foes at once. This charm may be activated so long as there is a secondary hostile target within close range of the original target, allowing the shot to bank off and attack the secondary target. If the target is a Strong type opponent the Dragonblooded makes a standard <b>withering </b>attack against the target, gaining no initiative from the attack. If the target is a Special type opponent (AKA: The game as normal) then the second carries a flat damage of the Dragonblooded\u2019s (Perception) which the damage cannot exceed her (Essence).<br /> <br /> At Essence 3+ this charm may be repurchased if the Dragonblooded knows Red Hot Demolition Round, allowing the Dragonblooded to activate this charm to immediately make a standard attack against the opponent. The Dragonblooded may choose to expend Fire Aura to waive the cost of this charm in such circumstances.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">HARVEST OF THE HUNTER</span><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: Book\u037e <b>Mins\u200b</b>: Archery 2 Essence 1\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Book<br /> <b>Keywords\u200b</b>: Air/Earth/Wood<br /> <b>Duration\u200b</b>: Book<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms\u200b</b>: None<br /> <br /> This charm is altered into Elemental aspects. One is chosen upon purchasing this charm, each additional one costs 3 XP.<ul><li>Air: The Dragonblooded becomes able to scavenge for energy cells or weapons that require energy in order to function. Any kind of energy can be used in order to power the weapon, and may plunge their hands into super intense burst of energy when activating their charm and take no damage, but anything more will prompt environmental resistance rolls. So long as there is a ready source of power after the battle (power outlet) then the Dragonblooded is able to fully charge his weapon(s).</li> <li>Earth: The Dragonblooded becomes able to scavenge for bullet based ammo. Any kind of stone or metal are able to become bullets of the Dragonblooded\u2019s weapon, and provided he has an access to stone or metal after a battle he is able to reload them all. Does not apply to explosive based weaponry.</li> <li>Wood: Remains the same</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">BRASS SENTINEL TECHNIQUE</span><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: 4m 1WP\u037e <b>Mins\u200b</b>: Archery 5 Essence 2\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: Air/Earth<br /> <b>Duration\u200b</b>: One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Harvest of the Hunter (Earth), Elemental Dragon Bullet<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded releases his weapon as it melts into the ground. Mild tremors are felt before a mound of stone rises from the ground with a perfectly carved replica of the scion\u2019s weapon resting on a swivel on top with an endless amount of bullets entering into it. This charm functions the same as Arbor Sentinel Technique, only it functions for Firearms and contains the Earth keyword. Energy weapons instead gain the Air keyword.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">STOKE-THE-FLAME FOCUS</span><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: - (+1a)\u037e <b>Mins\u200b</b>: Archery 5 Essence 2\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: Air/Fire<br /> <b>Duration\u200b</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Drawing the Lightning<br /> <br /> A swirling corona of flame forms around the muzzle of the Dragon-Blood\u2019s gun as he sights his target, growing in brilliance and intensity as he focuses. When he finally fires, the burning aura is discharged as a blazing fireball that engulfs the blast. This charm enhances the prerequisite, allowing it to be used for <b>withering </b>attacks, using the dice gained from aiming into the raw damage of the attack roll. This charm also allows the Dragonblooded to spend multiple turns aiming in order to increase the damage done to the target (<b>withering </b>only). For each turn spent aiming after the first the Dragonblooded needs to reactivate Drawing the Lightning and pay a 1a surcharge per turn after the first aiming cycle. The Dragonblooded can aim up to a maximum of (ESS/2, round up) times.<br /> <br /> If a Dragonblooded in a Fire (firearms) or Air (Bow) aura he may immediately complete a second aim action for the purposes of adding damage against a Strong type opponent.<br /> <br /> Lastly Drawing the Lightning gains the Fire keyword if the Dragonblooded uses Firearms with it, Air keyword for all other ranged weapons. For rule of cool the Air keyword can also apply to energy based weapons or railguns.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">BLAZING PHOENIX PINION</span><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: Book\u037e <b>Mins\u200b</b>: Archery 5 Essence 3\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Book<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: Book<br /> <b>Duration</b>\u200b: Book<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: None<br /> <br /> Strong type opponents caught in the blast are treated as being caught in a heavy explosion which increases the damage based on the amount of 10s in both the attack and damage roll.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">BOUGHS OF BURNING AUTUMN</span><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: Book\u037e <b>Mins\u200b</b>: Archery 4 Essence 1\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Book<br /> <b>Keywords\u200b</b>: Book<br /> <b>Duration\u200b</b>: Book<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Harvest of the Hunter<br /> <br /> This charm may be used to reflexively reload a Firearms weapon. Also to the people who told me a reflexive reload for a native Exalt charm would be stepping on Righteous Devil? HAHAHAHAHA!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T23:56:20-07:00","id":1206804,"title":"","content":"Although we don't have the complete list, all charms in the preview do have an Element entry in their keyword list, including Balanced charms. This seems to be a thing you should do also.<br /> <br /> Partial \u200bException: <i>Elusive Dragon-God Dispersion</i> places the keywords in the body text, as it changes effect depending on the aura aspect in which it is used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T00:23:18-07:00","id":1206806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206796-3e-dragonblooded-firearms-charms?p=1206804#post1206804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although we don't have the complete list, all charms in the preview do have an Element entry in their keyword list, including Balanced charms. This seems to be a thing you should do also.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elemental Bolt Attack has no elemental keywords. I'm assuming its element is whatever element you're casting it with. But since Elemental Dragon Bullet works in the same way I have that covered.<br /> <br /> All the other ones do. The Permanent charms use the original charm's element.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T01:10:39-07:00","id":1206814,"title":"","content":"Your version of Harvest of the Hunter should be &quot;Air or Earth or Wood&quot; not &quot;Air/Earth/Wood&quot;. They format it differently when you have to pick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T04:35:40-07:00","id":1206849,"title":"","content":"Oh sweet, this will help me get Roaring20s restarted when the time comes. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T10:04:46-07:00","id":1206927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206796-3e-dragonblooded-firearms-charms?p=1206814#post1206814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your version of Harvest of the Hunter should be &quot;Air or Earth or Wood&quot; not &quot;Air/Earth/Wood&quot;. They format it differently when you have to pick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked that, and the person I had check them said it was the slash version.<br /> <br /> I'll check later, but minor issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}